  "id": "Compound::DB06144 - Gene::3356",
  "verbalization": "Sertindole appears to interact with Htr2a through a shared pathway involving Htr1e, which participates in multiple biological processes. The evidence suggests that Sertindole binds to Htr1e, which then participates in serotonin receptor functions, and Htr2a is involved in the participation of these processes. This indicates a potential mechanism where Sertindole may influence Htr2a through its interaction with Htr1e, possibly by modulating the activity of serotonin receptors. The overlapping participation of Htr1e in different binding and receptor functions supports the idea that Sertindole could affect Htr2a via a common intermediary. The consistent binding to Htr1e across different paths strengthens the hypothesis that this interaction is central to the relationship between Sertindole and Htr2a.",
